# Normalise every text file to LF in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Added 20 August 2026. Without it, `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows checks files out with CRLF
# while agents working under WSL write LF, so git reports every line of every touched file as
# changed. Three agent branches came back with diffs of 913, 2,691 and 1,814 lines whose real
# content was 1, 9 and 48 lines. A diff nobody can read is a review nobody performs, and review
# time is the scarce resource here.
#
# This is not cosmetic. `docs/40-spec/v0-draft.md` §12 requires replay from the published
# fixture trajectory on Windows AND one non-Windows environment, so cross-platform byte
# agreement is a release condition, not a preference. `events.append()` already writes the
# trajectory with an explicit `newline="\n"`; this makes the rest of the tree agree with it.
#
# Reversal: delete this file and run `git add --renormalize .`.
# Falsifier: a file that genuinely requires CRLF to work would break. None is known — the only
# executable content is Python and shell — and any that appears should be pinned with an
# explicit `-text` or `eol=crlf` entry below rather than by removing the default.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly binary, so git never tries to normalise them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.db binary
*.sqlite binary
